# ~/.screenrc
#
# vim motions for the window list: C-a h goes left, C-a l goes right, which
# is what the fingers are already doing everywhere else.
#
# both letters were already spoken for, so each one's ctrl-twin takes in
# whatever got evicted:
#
#   C-a h    was hardcopy   -> prev.  hardcopy moves down to C-a C-h
#   C-a l    was redisplay  -> next.  redisplay was already on C-a C-l too,
#                                     so that one needed no help
#
# C-a C-h was a third way to say prev (screen 5 lists backspace, C-h, p and
# C-p for it), which is exactly why it was cheap to give away -- prev still
# answers to p, C-p and backspace, and next still answers to n, C-n and
# space. nothing here is the only route to anything.

bind h prev
bind ^h hardcopy
bind l next
